# Host-side port pi-web's iframe is served on (issue #3). When the host
# republishes it (an `sbx` sandbox mapping it to 30142, or a second instance
# reusing the port range), set the HOST port here so docker-compose both
# publishes it and tells the app to render the iframe URL with it. Unset =>
# 30141 (current behavior). NOTE the pairing: the iframe URL uses this port
# verbatim, and the browser reaches the sandbox only via `sbx ports`, so in
# the sbx scenario the HOST-side and sandbox-side ports must BOTH equal it:
# with PI_WEB_HOST_PORT=30142, compose binds 30142 inside the sandbox (30142
# -> container 30141), so publish the same port on both sides:
#   sbx ports <sandbox> --publish 30142:30142/tcp
# (NOT :30141 - nothing listens on 30141 in the sandbox when the variable is
# set; and not 30142:30141 for the same reason).
#PI_WEB_HOST_PORT=30142

# Gateway (caddy) entry port (issue #16). Drives BOTH the compose publish
# mapping and the Caddyfile site address (`:{$AIO_GATEWAY_PORT:8080}`, expanded
# inside the gateway container via env_file). Unset => 8080. Both sides of the
# mapping stay equal by construction, so `AIO_GATEWAY_PORT=8082 make up` serves
# everything (main UI / code-server / vnc) on 8082. NOTE in the `sbx` sandbox
# scenario the host-facing port is instead chosen by `sbx ports --publish`, so
# this variable usually only matters for bare `docker compose` deployments.
#AIO_GATEWAY_PORT=8082

